WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
Egypt and the Netherlands, drawn
on one map at the same scale.

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.450
Look at the two outlines.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.890
Now picture all the people
living inside each one.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.990
Seen from above, both have green farmland,

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.370
laid out in very different ways.

6
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.430
So which is more crowded?

7
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.870
Egypt, by far?

8
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.870
Or the Netherlands, by far?

9
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.190
In this mission, you'll calculate
how crowded each country really is,

10
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.180
using World Bank data from 2024.

11
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.590
Then you'll work out how much
farmland each person has,

12
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.610
and what happens when a
population outgrows its land.

13
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.590
Your mission: decide
which is more crowded,

14
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.870
Egypt or the Netherlands,
and justify your answer.
